bstring
------------------------------------------
The Better String Library is an abstraction of a string data type which is
superior to the C library char buffer string type. Among the features achieved are:
 * Substantial mitigation of buffer overflow/overrun problems and other
   failures that result from erroneous usage of the common C string library
   functions
 * Significantly simplified string manipulation
 * High performance interoperability with other source/libraries which expect
   '\0' terminated char buffers
 * Improved overall performance of common string operations
 * Functional equivalency with other more modern languages

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.11-1
  libbstring-devel-1.1.1-1bl1
  libbstring1-1.1.1-1bl1
  pkg-config-3.0.7-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.10-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  meson-1.9.2-1
  ninja-1.13.2-1

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/msteinert/bstring

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/msteinert/bstring/archive/refs/tags/v1.1.1.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack bstring-1.1.1-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./bstring-1.1.1-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/bstring-1.1.1-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/bstring-1.1.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libbstring1-1.1.1-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libbstring-devel-1.1.1-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

Files included in the binary package:

(bstring)
  /usr/share/doc/Cygwin/bstring.README
  /usr/share/doc/bstring/COPYING
  /usr/share/doc/bstring/README.md
  /usr/share/doc/bstring/comparisons.md
  /usr/share/doc/bstring/introduction.md
  /usr/share/doc/bstring/porting.md
  /usr/share/doc/bstring/security.md

(libbstring1)
  /usr/bin/cygbstring-1.dll

(libbstring-devel)
  /usr/include/bstraux.h
  /usr/include/bstrlib.h
  /usr/include/buniutil.h
  /usr/include/utf8util.h
  /usr/lib/libbstring.dll.a
  /usr/lib/pkgconfig/bstring.pc

